\f0\fs24 \cf0 ## double hashes demarcate unimplemented features\
\
Purpose: A lightweight simulation to demonstrate how traits adapt to environmental factors. Prey pursue food and randomly mutate predefined traits that benefit or detract from survivability while hunted by predators. Predators hunt and reproduce and mutate randomly as well, but can only consume prey. \
\
Prey\
2-5 \'93Species\'94 are spawned on map at start with randomly assigned trait values\
When prey eat food they spawn children that inherit the trait profile of parent with a percentage range of \'93mutation\'94 at a +/- value\
Each species starts as a color with each subsequent generation carrying a slightly variated iteration close to but different on the color pallet.\
## Keep species hue close to original on color pallet to show lineage (Blue, green, yellow, purple, pink)\
\
Predators\
Spawn in a red hue\
Can see slightly larger distance than prey\
## \'93lie in wait\'94 or camouflage function to reduce food loss per tick\
Once consuming prey, if the food is sufficiently high enough the predator will spawn a child\
Child will have slightly different hue along with mutated traits\
\
Map\
100x100 for now\
Intend to scale once algorithmic efficiencies are implemented to 200x200/300x300 or more\
## obstacles obstruct travel, adjacent (diagonal or side by side) tiles block movement through\
\
Sim Concepts (place wherever makes sense)\
Show real time dashboard information of creature demographics and trends\
Pathfinding for each entity to object of interest within vision radius\
Deconfliction of priorities (move to closest food or run from predator if encountered on way to food)}